  "created": "2026-09-02T17:09:24.457Z",
  "description": "Avalonia LinuxFramebuffer support for the ifm CR1140/CR1141 (ecomatDisplay 4.3\", NXP i.MX 8M Nano / aarch64): a custom IInputBackend (EvdevKeypadInput) that reads the gpio-keys keypad from /dev/input/event1 (evdev) — Avalonia's built-in LinuxFramebuffer input handles touch/pointer only, so keypad-only SKUs need this — a SoftKeyFooter control with physical-keypad or natural (F1..F6) ordering, and a framework-agnostic SystemTelemetry collector (CPU, memory, SoC/board temperature, uptime, load) plus DeviceInfo (hostname, os-release, eth0/can0 state) read from /proc and sysfs. Dual-licensed: GPL-3.0-only, or commercial from UpTux UG.",
  "id": "Cr1140.Avalonia",
